# Redakt → Presidio fork pinning record
#
# This file records which Presidio fork branch + commit SHA range the
# Redakt repo is paired with. It exists to give cross-repo traceability
# without requiring a git submodule (CLAUDE.md: `presidio/` is a fork
# checkout, not a submodule). When a Redakt commit assumes specific
# fork-side behavior, the corresponding fork SHA(s) MUST appear here so
# a future bisect across either repo can recover the pairing.
#
# Format:
#   feature: <SDD feature ID>
#   branch:  <fork branch name>
#   commits: <oldest-fork-SHA>..<newest-fork-SHA>  (range, inclusive)
#   notes:   <one-line rationale>
#
# Update this file in the same Redakt commit that lands a fork-side
# change. If a fork commit is amended or rebased, update the SHA here
# too (keeps the pairing intact).

feature: 007 (transformers-nlp-backend)
branch:  main
commits: 1070180..2fbe4d9
notes:   MultiNlpEngine + multi.yaml + Dockerfile.multi + revision pin
         (chunks 1A, 1B, 5, 4c). 4e adds populated digest manifest +
         tamper test + atomic manifest write + retry-after-failure +
         schema validator annotation. Originally developed on a feature
         branch (`feature/redakt-007-multi-nlp-engine`) on a separate
         machine; that branch was consumed into `main` and not retained
         on origin. 15ceffd is post-completion image-slim (-51.7%):
         CPU-only torch + HF Hub alt-framework prune + manifest
         re-baseline. 4b24175 extends DE_PLZ recognizer context with
         common German street suffixes (weg/allee/ring/platz/gasse/etc.)
         to fix address-block recall in the Memodo calibration pilot.
         322eccf adds DeMastrRecognizer (DE_MASTR_ID, 3-letter prefix +
         12 digits MaStR-Nummer per BNetzA) and scopes
         MedicalLicenseRecognizer to en only — together closing the
         MaStR recall miss and the MEDICAL_LICENSE-on-German-text
         spurious surfaced by the same pilot. f19a6b6 patches DE_PLZ
         CONTEXT for the spaCy de_core_news_sm lemma drift on
         "Lieferadresse" -> "Lieferadres" (over-aggressive -esse
         stripping); adds the observed broken lemma so the +0.35
         context boost finally applies on bare "Lieferadresse: <PLZ>"
         positives. cff328a extends DE_PLZ CONTEXT with bare
         "anschrift" plus the B2B project anchors "bauvorhaben" /
         "baustelle" — closes the "<project word> in <PLZ> <City>"
         shape (Memodo pilot phrase 02 — Bauvorhaben in 73230
         Kirchheim/Teck), the sole remaining DE_PLZ recall miss after
         the prior two CONTEXT fixes. ee93662 splits DateRecognizer's
         dd.mm.yyyy pattern into a 4-digit-year form at 0.95 (clears
         consumer DATE_TIME floors meant to drop NLP overfire) + a
         2-digit form at 0.4 (ambiguous with software versions); adds
         German date keywords to CONTEXT. Closes 4/6 DATE_TIME misses
         on German requests (xlm-roberta has no DATE label, so the
         regex is the only signal). 587957a adds EuVatIdRecognizer
         (EU_VAT_ID) — one multi-country recognizer covering all 27
         EU prefixes at 0.5 base score, registered for both en and de
         so cross-border B2B traffic between a German HQ and its
         IT/CZ/NL subsidiaries (or English correspondence mentioning
         Austrian or Polish suppliers) yields detections on non-DE
         prefixes that DeVatIdRecognizer never handled. Per-prefix
         body lengths from the VIES spec; lookaround anchors prevent
         matches from extending into adjacent alphanumeric tokens.
         DeVatIdRecognizer is unchanged and remains the de-only
         authority on DE-prefixed IDs (both fire on DE prefix; the
         score merge yields one result per span). 2fbe4d9 caps
         transformers <5.0 + huggingface_hub <1.0 in
         presidio-analyzer/pyproject.toml. Both v5/v1 majors shipped
         on 2026-05-11 and have not yet been validated end-to-end
         against `spacy_huggingface_pipelines` 0.0.4 or the SDD-007
         MultiNlpEngine + xlm-roberta path; the caps pin docker
         rebuilds to the same version set the calibration baseline
         was anchored on. Remove the caps after an eval-suite +
         calibration-report re-anchor on the new majors. SHA range
         is the authoritative anchor.
